{"metadata": {"version": "0.3.3", "copyright": "Copyright (c) 2026 graineo project; format and method by Andrea Volpato (spektrafilm). Licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.", "created": "2026-10-29", "license": "spektrafilm profile by Andrea Volpato, licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Redistribution and derivatives must credit the author, link the project (https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm),preserve this license, and remain CC BY-SA 4.0.Modifications must be noted. Full text of the license and attribution requirements: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm/blob/main/SPEKTRAFILM_LICENSE.txt.", "citation": "If you use this profile in your work, please cite the spektrafilm project: https://github.com/andreavolpato/spektrafilm, see CITATION.cff for details.", "datasource": "Characteristic curves (Status M, CN-16), spectral sensitivity (blue, green and red sensitive layers) and spectral dye density curves (mid-scale neutral and minimum density) digitised from raster images of the Fujifilm data sheet AF3-026E (FUJICOLOR SUPERIA 200, page 4). Original data are property of Fujifilm Corporation. The fourth (cyan sensitive) layer is not represented. Exposure axis shifted by log10(14.5/200) so that 0 is mid-grey at ISO 200. Density scale a, standard dyes and adaptation window follow the graineo colour-negative family rule derived from official spektrafilm profiles (Fujifilm C200, X-TRA 400, Pro 400H). Derived from spektrafilm profile format; modified by graineo.", "modifications": "New profile created from manufacturer data by the graineo project; only the profile format, wavelength grid and the family dye/window constants taken from spektrafilm profiles."}, "info": {"type": "negative", "support": "film", "stage": "filming", "use": "still", "antihalation": "weak", "target_print": "fujifilm_crystal_archive_typeii", "channel_model": "color", "densitometer": "status_M", "log_sensitivity_density_over_min": 1.0, "reference_illuminant": "D55", "viewing_illuminant": "D50", "name": "Fujifilm Superia 200", "card": {"maker": "Fujifilm", "iso": 200, "type": "Farbnegativfilm", "additional": "Datenblatt AF3-026E, RMS 4 (Fuji-Skala)", "text": "Der Fuji-Alltagsfilm der Superia-Reihe: etwas kontrastreicher und satter als C200, mit k\u00fchlerem, leicht gr\u00fcnlichem Grundton. Kurven und Spektren stammen aus Rasterbildern des Datenblatts; die vierte Farbschicht des Films ist nicht abgebildet.", "source": "Fujifilm AF3-026E", "process": "C-41 (auch Fuji CN-16)", "period": "Kleinbildfilm 2017 eingestellt (best\u00e4tigt Mai 2017, Vorrat bis Anfang 2018)", "suitable": ["Alltag und Reise bei Tageslicht", "Stra\u00dfe", "Portr\u00e4t am Tag"], "less_suitable": ["Kunstlicht ohne Blitz", "gro\u00dfe Vergr\u00f6\u00dferungen"], "tips": ["Wirkt der Grundton zu k\u00fchl: W\u00e4rme im Abzug leicht nach warm schieben.", "Mit \u201eFujifilm C200\u201c im Vergleichen-Modus nebeneinanderlegen: der Superia ist satter und kontrastreicher."], "facts": [{"text": "Die Superia-Reihe erschien um 1998 als Nachfolger der Super-G-plus-Filme und f\u00fchrte eine vierte Farbschicht f\u00fcr bessere Farben unter Leuchtstofflicht ein. Die Einstellung des Superia 200 in 135 wurde im Mai 2017 best\u00e4tigt.", "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fujifilm_Superia"}]}, "stock": "fujifilm_superia_200"}, "data": {"wavelengths": [380.0, 385.0, 390.0, 395.0, 400.0, 405.0, 410.0, 415.0, 420.0, 425.0, 430.0, 435.0, 440.0, 445.0, 450.0, 455.0, 460.0, 465.0, 470.0, 475.0, 480.0, 485.0, 490.0, 495.0, 500.0, 505.0, 510.0, 515.0, 520.0, 525.0, 530.0, 535.0, 540.0, 545.0, 550.0, 555.0, 560.0, 565.0, 570.0, 575.0, 580.0, 585.0, 590.0, 595.0, 600.0, 605.0, 610.0, 615.0, 620.0, 625.0, 630.0, 635.0, 640.0, 645.0, 650.0, 655.0, 660.0, 665.0, 670.0, 675.0, 680.0, 685.0, 690.0, 695.0, 700.0, 705.0, 710.0, 715.0, 720.0, 725.0, 730.0, 735.0, 740.0, 745.0, 750.0, 755.0, 760.0, 765.0, 770.0, 775.0, 780.0], "log_sensitivity": [[-4.253559669209289, -3.1217857429955824, -0.9151196487907236], [-4.2535